\f3\fs26 The laceration on Johnny\'92s scalp was long and deep and he was moaning loudly, continuously and infuriatingly. It was still seeping blood, but had settled down sufficiently to allow debriding of any remaining debris. The jagged edges were brought together, and held tight for the application of the fast-heal gel, finally shutting the gaping wound. He wailed like a banshee, lamenting the scar that would no doubt form, but he felt adequately rested to re-commence his rudimentary examination of the disc.\
\'93You were right about the Faraday Cage. It doesn\'92t stop the disc operating, but it inhibits the effects.\'94 The Johnny placed the disc on a kitchen bench and managed to capture about 30 images on his palm device. The resolution allowed him to blow up the images many thousands of times, zooming in on the fine detail. \'93Even though the bio-circuits are still regenerating, or at least they appear to be, the disc is presently dormant. I would not have been able to capture any images otherwise. The bio-matter appears to be alive, but it cannot be. I can offer no explanation.\'94 The Johnny was most perplexed. He then place it in the palm of his hand and squashed it down hard, just like his grandma forcing a valueless copper coin into his hand as a kid. \'93I can feel it heating up, but it doesn\'92t want to bite into me. Give me your hand Sarah.\'94 \
 \
Sarah placed her forearm on the bench, palm up and The Johnny, with the disc held between thumb and forefinger, slowly lowered nearer. He allowed it to touch her skin momentarily, withdrawing it to hover a few millimetres above her skin. Tiny tendrils reached out, desperately trying to make contact with flesh and presumably, dig in deep.\
\'93Now you.\'94 The Johnny said to Cracker.\
\'93You may call me Mr Hardy.\'94 Cracker offered up his palm. The disc was equally anxious to penetrate his calloused skin and get at the flesh beneath.\
\'93It does not make sense. What is the difference between you two and me?\'94 The Johnny didn\'92t like being left out, but Sarah already knew what had happened. The disc\'92s bio-matter was inanimate until it came into direct contact with her and the virus she carried. In infecting the bio-matter, the nature of the disc must have been altered, she opined. Lamenting her ignorance of micro-biology, her brain filled with scenarios and outcomes, all of which resulted in disaster. Vacantly altering this technology could not be good.\
\'93So, am I going to turn into a cyborg?\'94 Cracker giggled, breaking into jerky, staccato movement. \'93Check it, I would make a great mechanoid.\'94\
\'93Cyborg? I doubt it, but I promise nothing.\'94 The Johnny replied.\
\'93What about robo-tit?\'94 Cracker asked, waiting for laughs that would never come.\
\'93All healed and nothing untoward, so far.\'94 Sarah replied. Her ability to ignore his crudeness amazed The Johnny who wanted to scream every time Cracker opened his mouth.\
\'93Can I have a look?\'94 Cracker was eternally optimistic.\
\'93No! You have seen enough!\'94 She had no plans to expose herself to anyone in the foreseeable future.\
\'93I just want to make sure it\'92s not going septic.\'94 Cracker figured it never hurt to ask.\
\'93What now?\'94 The Johnny just wanted to go home and forget about everything. He had no interest in reporting anything to anyone, fuck company policy. His foray into the world of the working class had been an unmitigated disaster, a mistake he would not be making again, not even for Sarah.\
\'93I suggest you keep the disc Johnny. It seems to pose no danger to you. Storage arrangements at your discretion, but ensure that it cannot be found. Do you agree?\'94 Sarah decided these guys needed some managing.\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93I think it would be dangerous to use it for any purpose, it may not operate to factory specifications anymore. It might very well be disastrous. For the time being, just safely store it.\'94 \
\'93What about us? We both have that phony DNA in us.\'94 Cracker hoped the plan involved spending more time with Sarah. \
\'93I am still very reluctant to seek medical advice, but one of us should.\'94\
\'93Both of us should. I know someone who can arrange pathology tests if we score her some decent patches. It\'92ll take a while to organise, but I should be able to swing it. \'94 Cracker\'92s cleaning contracts had given him access to a broad range of flawed characters across the entire dominion. \
 \
\'93Okay, I will see if I can come along, too. How fast can you arrange it?\'94 Sarah knew it would be difficult to get away from work for a while.\
\'93It will take a few days to get all my ducks in a row. I will have to get my hands on premium patches and I\'92ll have to catch her at work, she\'92ll be tripping balls the rest of the time. If I can get hold of a \'93Surprise Party\'94 or two she\'92ll be happy. I don\'92t know her schedule, so yeah, I think a few days ought to do it.\'94\
\'93It would be preferable if it were sooner, but I fear my schedule will demand all my attention for a week at least. I\'92ve just signed a new contract.\'94 Sarah revealed.\
\'93New gig? Excellent, Sarah. Where?\'94 Johnny really wanted details of her remuneration package, specifically whether it was better that his. \
\'93I can\'92t say. Confidentiality, you know the drill.\'94 She was way ahead of him.\
\'93Yep. I wish you luck. Starting a new contract is always tough at first.\'94 Johnny seemed genuine, but he really had to find out what she was earning. \
\'93I\'92ll make arrangements. How are we to keep in touch? I don\'92t suppose either of you will want my ident appearing in your com-records?\'94 Cracker figured he had better get back in his place.\
\'93I\'92ll contact you.\'94 Sarah said. \'93Johnny you get back to work and make discreet inquiries with your colleagues, but remember there are ruthless men searching for the disc. Do not expose yourself.\'94\uc0\u8232 \
\'93I will just keep an ear out. That\'92s all.\'94 The Johnny gently touched the dressing on his head and then looked around the room in disgust. \'93I am going home and forgetting about all of this. Die horribly Mr Hardy, failing that, I hope never to see you again.\'94 With that he stood up and walked to the door and then back again. \'93Sarah? I have no idea where I am. Take me home.\'94\
\'93Such a baby.\'94 Sarah sighed. \'93Okay. Don\'92t forget to cage up the disc.\'94 She stood before Cracker, smiled warmly and slapped him in the face. \'93That\'92s for latching onto my boob and this\'85.\'94 She kissed him gently on the lips. Cracker wanted to invade the poignancy with tongue, but much to his disgust, he suffered another attack of impulse control. \'93\'85is for saving my life. You dragged me out of the fire and delivered me to safety and it is something I will not forget.\'94\
\'93I had forgotten about the bomb. I guess I will be occupied with a few funerals, over the next week or so.\'94\
\'93Bomb? What have you two been up to?\'94 Johnny shook his head. \
\'93Do you really want to know?\'94 Sarah asked, unsmiling.\
\'93No. I do not think I do.\'94\
\'93I don\'92t think our adventure is over yet.\'94 Cracker hoped he would not cry until she left, but he could not hold out and he let a couple of tears escape down his cheeks. \
\'93I am so sorry.\'94 She hugged him gently and squished herself into his chest. \'93Three good friends, your loss must be terrible.\'94\
He didn\'92t tell her, but he cried not for the passing of his friends, but at the thought of her leaving. The death of a few friends was nothing compared to the anguish of being denied her presence. 
